
A list of problems that a programming language should enable solving:


* We must be able to generate code that can also be referenced from the frontend.

Generating code on the level of IR is all well and good,
but we also need to be able to generate code that can then be used in the fronted,
like functions that can be called by an identifier, enumerations and variables.

* We do also want to be able to add meta-code in the middle of a procedure.

Something like:

switch type {
    ${
        for type in types {
            name := type.name;
            *{
                case types.$(types.value): {
                    print("{$name}\n");
                }
            *}
        }
    $}
}

* Instead of macros we should have generating functions,
  but then we need to differentiate between which function is a generator and which not,
  so that when we call it we call it during parsing and vice versa.

float
normal_func(i = int, d = float)
{
    return float(3 * i) / d;
}

$gen
print(args = ...)
{
    ..
}


